Subject: [PATCH] Preserve CPU warp rotation trig across the finite float domain

Port historical ProjectM TV patch 0051 (PR #51, release v2.3.17) to
projectM 4.2 master. MilkDrop 2's milkdropfs.cpp computes sinf/cosf after
converting the evaluated rotation to float. The observed Apple GLES
translator returns zero for both functions at +/-10000000 even at highp.
CPU libm also handles FLT_MAX, where a double 2*pi remainder is insufficient.
Keep authored equation state and nonfinite behavior unchanged.

4.2 uses separate VertexBuffers rather than 4.1.7's interleaved MeshVertex.
Reuse transforms.z for sine and add one four-byte cosine buffer at attribute
8 (seven consumed warp attributes, within GLES 3.0's required minimum).
Resize/upload it with the existing buffers so Prepare/DrawAgain retain the
same evaluated mesh. Cache per-frame trig when no per-pixel code is present.
No public C/Java/JNI API or preset changes. Other shader trig is unchanged.

